# meta-lastandfast

Lastandfast custom Yocto layer for the INAR robotic arm.
Target: NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano (jetson-orin-nano-devkit)

## Partition Layout

| Partition | Mount | Type | Mode |
|-----------|-------|------|------|
| mmcblk0p1 | / (slot A) | ext4 | read-only |
| mmcblk0p2 | / (slot B) | ext4 | read-only |
| mmcblk0p3 | /data | ext4 | read-write |

## OTA Strategy

A/B partition scheme. Active slot selected by bootloader (CBoot/U-Boot).
Updates written to inactive slot. Rollback automatic on boot failure.
/etc/fstab uses /dev/root (bootloader-resolved) not hardcoded partition.

## Build Instructions

1. Install Yocto dependencies (Ubuntu 22.04)
2. Clone layers:
   - poky (scarthgap)
   - meta-openembedded (scarthgap)
   - meta-tegra (scarthgap)
   - meta-lastandfast (this repo)
3. source poky/oe-init-build-env build
4. bitbake core-image-minimal

## Flash Instructions

cd build/tmp/deploy/images/jetson-orin-nano-devkit
tar xf core-image-minimal-jetson-orin-nano-devkit.rootfs.tegraflash.tar.gz
sudo ./doflash.sh

## Adding a New Machine Target (e.g. Orin NX)

In conf/local.conf change:
MACHINE = "jetson-orin-nano-devkit"
to:
MACHINE = "jetson-orin-nx-devkit"

All recipes in meta-lastandfast are machine-agnostic and will work unchanged.
